<title>USA: U.S. Jan retail sales rose 0.6 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Jan retail sales rose 0.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Jan    Dec-(Prev)  Jan97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.6    0.3   0.6     4.9</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.4   Unch   0.6     4.6</p>
<p> Auto Sales		1.2    1.0   0.7     5.7</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.7    0.2   0.5     6.0</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.5    0.3   0.7     4.2</p>
<p> Furniture Stores	0.6   -0.8   0.1     3.7</p>
<p> Building Materials    1.2   -0.8  -1.6     9.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Jan     Dec-(Previous)    Nov--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 209.05   207.87  208.19   207.32  206.97</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    157.33   156.77  157.30   156.74  156.42</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    51.72    51.10   50.89    50.58   50.55</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 85.44    84.82   84.95    84.60   84.56</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   123.62   123.05  123.24   122.72  122.41</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.39    11.33   11.47    11.41   11.45</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.21    11.08   10.95    11.17   11.13</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Jan    Dec-(Prev)  Jan97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores  1.3    0.8   0.5     6.1</p>
<p> Department Stores     1.3    1.7   0.9     7.6</p>
<p> Food Stores	    Unch    0.2   0.3     2.2</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	 -0.1    0.2   0.4     2.0</p>
<p> Gas Stations	    0.9    0.4   0.8     6.6</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 -0.9    0.4   1.5    -0.3</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places	0.6   -0.4  -0.3     3.7</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.7    0.4   0.7     8.5</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Jan     Dec-(Previous)     Nov---(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    26.45    26.10    26.02     25.90   25.88</p>
<p> Department Stores   20.85    20.58    20.36     20.24   20.18</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.76    35.75    35.84     35.68   35.73</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.82    33.85    33.98     33.78   33.84</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.45    13.33    13.33     13.29   13.23</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.21     9.29     9.43	9.25    9.29</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.31    20.18    19.91     20.26   19.98</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    7.73     7.68     7.70	7.65    7.65</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected January retail sales to rise 0.7 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>The department said that despite the downward revised December data, there was no change in the 5.3 percent rise previously reported for all of 1996.</p>
<p>The department revised November retail sales to a 0.1 percent decrease from a 0.2 percent drop. November sales excluding autos were revised to a 0.2 percent increase from being unchanged. November auto sales were revused to a 0.9 percent decrease from down 1.0 percent.</p>
